abstract: >-
  Tools for obtaining the full-resolution BodyParts3D / Anatomography version
  4.3 anatomical mesh set, which no published archive or documented Web API
  distributes: the bulk archive ships only the 99% polygon-reduced version 4.0,
  and the documented API returns rendered images rather than geometry. A
  downloader drives the Anatomography viewer's own endpoints and pins the
  result to version 4.3 by seeding it from the version-stamped 4.3 manifest,
  then verifies that every declared element is present and loadable. A subset
  selector takes named groups of elements by regular expression over their
  Foundational Model of Anatomy names, so that a whole organ can be requested
  even where version 4.3 supplies it only in parts - the cerebrum as gyri, the
  lung as bronchopulmonary segments, the heart as chamber walls. The verified
  3,210-mesh set is included.
